  "description": "Acute electrocorticography recorded from two epilepsy surgery patients during a speech prediction task, minutes before and after neurosurgical disconnection of the left anterior temporal lobe (a semantic hub). Recordings cover a frontal grid, temporal pole, subtemporal and lateral temporal strips, and a Heschl's gyrus depth electrode. This BIDS derivative repackages the Zenodo release as BrainVision files, with downsampled (1000 Hz) and denoised (demodulated band transform plus first-SVD-component removal) versions, along with events and electrode tables.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG was sampled at 2000 Hz and downsampled to 1000 Hz. Denoising used the demodulated band transform and removal of the first SVD component. Recordings were made at least 20 min after anaesthesia stopped, before and after left ATL disconnection, using a frontal grid (96 or 64 contacts), temporal pole, subtemporal and lateral temporal strips, and an 8-contact Heschl's gyrus depth electrode. Data were converted to BrainVision float32 with events and electrode tables.",
